n(d) whether the Governme nt has warned these States for failing to spend the funds\nallocated under the healthcare schemes and if so, the details thereof, State-wise; and\n(e) whether the Government has issued any directions and guidelines in this regard and if\nso, the details the reof along with the steps taken by the Government to monitor the\nimplementation of Centrally Sponsored Schemes and utilisation of funds by the States?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI JAGAT PRAKASH NADDA)\n(a) to (e) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 101* FOR 22TH DECEMBER, 2017\n(a) Per capita expenditure on healthcare by Government (Centre and States)\nfor last three years and current year, at current prices, is estimated as under:\n(i) 2014-15 - Rs. 1108\n(ii) 2015-16 - Rs. 1251\n(iii) 2016-17  (RE) - Rs. 1526\n(iv) 2017-18 (BE) - Rs. 1797\n(b) The Government has recently released data relating to National Health\nAccounts (NHA) 2014-15 and the key health financing indicators for India: NHA\nEstimates 2014-15 is  given at Annexure-I.\n(c) & (d) The State -wise release of funds and expenditure under the National\nHealth Mission (NHM) is provided at Annexure-II. A few States failed to\nutilize the released funds expeditiously. Letters were issued to the concerned\nState Governments   to utilize the funds expeditiously.\n(e) Public Health being a State subject, primary responsibility of implementation\nand monitoring of schemes under NHM rests with the State Governments.\nHowever, details of steps taken by the Central Government to monitor the\nimplementation of NHM and utilization of funds by the States are provided at\nAnnexure-III.\n\nAnnexure -I\nThe key health financing indicators for India: NHA Estimates 2014-15\nSl.\nNo.\nIndicator NHA  2014-15\n1 Total Health Expenditure (THE) as % GDP$ 3.89\n2 THE per capita (Rs.)# 3826\n3 Government Health Expenditure (GHE) as % of THE 