    (श्री अरुण जेटली) \n \n(a) to (d) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF THE \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 264 FOR ANSWER IN LOK SABHA  \nON 05.01.2018 \n \n(a): As per section 73 of Companies Act, 2013 r/w Companies \n(Acceptance of Deposits) Rules 2014, the private company is \npermitted to accept deposits from its Directors & their relatives and \nalso up to certain limit from its members only.  Therefore, a Private \nCompany is not eligible to accept public deposits u/s 76 r/w the \nCompanies (Acceptance of Deposit) Rules, 2014. \n \nHowever, various Complaints in respect of violations of terms & \nconditions of the deposits have been received by respective \nRegistrars of Companies (ROCs) against 24 No. of Private Companies \nas per the provisions of Companies Act, 1956/2013.  A statement \ncontaining names of such companies for last three financial year is \nenclosed herewith as Annexure - A. \n \n(b) & (c): Prosecutions under the provisions of the Companies Act, \n1956/2013 have been filed against the 4 companies involving 15 \ncases, which are sub -judice, and in other cases the matter is under \nexamination or at inquiry/ inspection stage.   \n \n(d): Till date no person has been jailed for aforesaid offences. \n \n******* \n\n  \nAnnexure - A \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO THE STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 264 FOR ANSWER IN LOK SABHA ON 05.01.2018. \n \nLIST OF PRIVATE LIMITED COMPANIES AGAINST WHICH \nCOMPLAINTS RECEIVED DURING THE LAST THREE YEARS: \n \n2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 \n \n1) Achal Automobiles Pvt. \nLtd. \n \n2) Car Source India Pvt \nLtd \n \n3) Escalations Travel ware \nIndia Private Limited \n \n4) KBC Multitrade Private \nLimited \n \n5) Veronica Construction \nPrivate Limited \n \n6) Starnet Breeding and \nResearch Farms Private \nLimited \n \n7) Staywell infoteh Private \nLimited \n \n8) Gayathri Bricks Private \nLimited \n \n9) Makhouse Infratech \nPrivate Limited \n \n1. Kapil Consultancy \nServices Pvt Ltd.  \n \n2. Kapil Foods \nStructure Pvt Ltd. \n \n3. Kapil Chits (Kosta) \nPvt. Ltd. \n \n4. Kapil Infra Avenues \nPvt. Ltd. \n \n5. Hira retail \n(Hyderabad Pvt. Ltd) \n \n6. New look Retails \nPrivate Limited \n \n7. Tulip Global Private \nLimited \n \n8. Preeya Homes Study \nPrivate Limited \n \n1 Vipachi \nBuilders \nDevelopers Pvt. \nLtd. \n \n2. Royal Twinkle \nStars Club \nPrivate Limited \n \n3. Bulmen \nMarketing \nPrivate Limited \n \n4. My Recharge \nPrivate Limited \n \n5. Paynut digital \nPrivate Limited \n \n6. Young  \nAttitude \nPropcon Private \nLimited \n \n7. Kuldeep Real \nTradex Private \nLimited \n \n\n \n******* \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|13|STARRED   |265", "t": "Compensation to States", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUN-STARRED QUESTION NO. 265 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18TH DECEMBER, 2017 \n                               \nINTERNET ACCESS FACILITATION \n \n265.  SHRI PARVESH SAHIB SINGH: \n \n(a) whether career counselling as envisaged under the National Career Service Project is \navailable to those who do not have access to online facilities, if so, the details thereof; \n(b) whether those who are financially incapable of regular access to online facilities can \navail information on c areer opportunities via convenient means, if so, the details \nthereof; \n(c) whether the Government is aware that there are job applicants who do not have \nregular access to internet and world wide web in order to check job opportunities and \nif so, the details thereof; \n(d) whether the Government has planned any measures to facilitate internet access to \nthose who cannot afford it; and \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR FOR EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR GANGWAR) \n \n(a) to (c):  The Ministry is implementing the National Career Service (NCS) Project as a \nMission Mode Project for transformation of the National Employment Service to provide a \nvariety of employment related services such as career counselling, vocational guidance, \nproviding information on skill development courses etc. The NCS is an online portal \n(www.ncs.gov.in) and is supported by a centralized multi lingual help desk.  \nThe services of NCS are accessible to all irrespective of ac cessibility to internet \nconnectivity. The NCS services can also be availed directly through the Employment \nExchanges, Model Career Centres, Common Service Centres and Post Offices.  \n(d) to (e):  In order to improve internet/ broadband facilities, BharatNet  project has been \nplanned to provide 100 Mbps broadband connectivity to all Gram Panchayats (approx. 2.5 \nlakh) in the country by using an optimal mix of underground fibre, fibre over power lines, \nradio and satellite media. Under first phase of the project,  1 lakh Gram Panchayats (GPs) \nare to be connected by laying underground Optical Fibre Cable(OFC) which is under \nimplementation. Under Phase-II, connectivity will be provided to remaining 1.5 lakh GPs in \nthe country using an optimal mix of underground fibre , fibre over power lines, radio and \nsatellite media. Provision of last mile access to the network and broadband service \nprovisioning shall be through Wi -Fi or any other broadband access technologies in all \n2,50,000 GPs in the country. \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|13|STARRED   |266", "t": "Depleting Forest Coverage", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 266\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.12.2017\n \n \nINCLUSION OF CHENNAI IN UNESCO LIST\n \n \n266. SHRI C. MAHENDRAN:\n \n \nWill the Minister of CULTURE be pleased to state :\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether Chennai was recently i\nncluded in United Nations \nEducational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNESCO) creative \ncities network for contribution in Music;\n \n \n(b)\n \n \nif so, the details thereof;\n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether this will foster international cooperation with and between \ncities commi\ntted to investing in creativity as a driver for sustainable \nurban development, social inclusion and cultural vibrancy and if so, \nthe details thereof; and\n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether the Government has any special arrangements to utilize this \ninternational recognition an\nd if so, the details thereof ?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR CULTURE\n \nAND\n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST & CLIMATE CHANGE\n \n \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA)\n \n(a) to (d) Yes Madam. On 31st October 2017, Director General of UNESCO \ndesignated Chennai as Crea\ntive City of Music under UNESCO's Creative \nCities Network. The creative cities Network of UNESCO aims to strengthen \nCooperation with and among cities that have recognised creativity as a \nstrategic factor of sustainable development as regards economic, soci\nal, \ncultural and environmental aspects. By joining the Network the government \nproposes to acknowledge the commitment of Chennai to share best \npractices to develop partnerships fostering international cooperation that \npromote Creativity and the Cultural ind\nustries to strengthen\n \nparticipation in \ncultural life and to integrate Culture in urban development plans.\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|13|STARRED   |267", "t": "Women Entrepreneurs under MUDRA Yojana", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 267 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18TH DECEMBER, 2017 \nIMPORT OF OIL AND PETROLEUM PRODUCTS \n267. SHRIMATI V. SATHYA BAMA:  \n        SHRI BHARATHI MOHAN R.K.:  \n        SHRI PR. SENTHIL NATHAN \n \n�������������������������������� �� ������������������������ \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government  proposes to develop integrated  petroleum and oil and gas zones  in the country and if  so, the \ndetails thereof along with number of such zones created during the last three years and the current year;  \n(b) whether the Government has  chalked out any comprehensive strategy  to make India self -reliant in the oil, gas and  \npetroleum sector and to reduce import of oil and other petroleum products and if so, the details thereof; and  \n(c) the quantum of petroleum products and crude oil imported and total expenditure incurred thereon in terms of rupee and \ndollar during the last  three years  and the current year,  product/country-wise including United States of America and  \nMiddle East Countries? \nANSWER \n�������������������������������� �� �������������������������� ������������������������������ �\nMINISTER OF PETROLEUM & NATURAL GAS (SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n(a) ONGC has got conducted a feasibility study for examining the possibility of establishment of Petroleum Economic Zone \n(PEZ) in the country. \n(b) The roadmap for reduction of import of crude oil, petroleum products and natural gas dependence broadly comprises \nfive-pronged strategy: \nI.� Increasing production of oil and gas; \nII.� Promoting energy efficiency and conservation measures; \n\nIII.� Giving thrust on demand substitution; \nIV.� Capitalizing untapped potential in biofuels and other alternate fuels/ renewables and; \nV.� Implementing measures for refinery process improvements. \n(c) Details of the quantum of petroleum products an d crude oil imported and total expenditure incurred in terms of rupees \ncrore and billion dollar during the last three years and the current year 2014 -15 to 2016-17 and 2017-18 (April to October) \nare given in Table-1 of Annexure.  \nThe details of country-wise petroleum products and region-wise/ country-wise crude oil imports during 2014-15 to 2016-17 \nand 2017-18 (April to October) are given in Table-2 and Table-3 of Annexure. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������