f Junior Medical Record \nTechnicians in Employees’ State Insurance Corporation in various States \nhas been conducted in the recent past;  \n(b)if so, the details thereof;  \n(c)whether all the appointments have been made in accordance with the laid \ndown eligibility conditions; and  \n(d)if so, the details thereof along with the number of candidates appointed, \nState/UT-wise?  \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR GANGWAR) \n(a) & (b):  Yes, Madam.  The ESIC conducted Online Examination for \nrecruitment to the post of Junior Medical Record Technician in the year 2016 \nas under: \nSl. No. Name of the State \n1. Punjab \n2. Haryana \n3. Kerala \n4. West Bengal \n \n(c) & (d):  No, Madam.  As per provision contained in Recruitment Rules, \nthe selection  process for the post of Junior Medical Record Technician is \nprescribed as under:  \nStage I – Online Exam. \nStage II – Computer Test on Working Knowledge of Computer as per \nrequirement of Recruitment Regulations for the post. \nBased on online examination, the candidates have been shortlisted for stage-\nII examination i.e. the Computer Test on the basis of their performance.    \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|13|UNSTARRED |314", "t": "Performance of Central Universities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 314 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.12.2017 \nPerformance of Central Universities \n \n314.  SHRI JAGDAMBIKA PAL: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of Central Universities presently functioning in the country; \n \n(b) whether the Government has evaluated the performance of the Central Universities on various \nparameters like content, quality, research, innovation, faculty development and affirmative action; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the details of the directives issued by the University Grants \nCommission (UGC) for implementation of reservation policy for Scheduled Castes/Scheduled Tribes \nin aca demic and non -academic posts in the Central Universities and the extent to which they have \nbeen implemented; and \n \n(d) the concrete steps being taken by the Government to improve the performance of the Central \nUniversities in the country? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(DR. SATYA PAL SINGH) \n \n(a)  At present, there are 41 Central Universities under the purview of this Ministry.  \n \n(b) & (c ) :Issues relating to improvement of quality of education, promoting research \nand innova tion, faculty development, collaboration with the industry and research \nlaboratories, effective use of technology in teaching -learning process, mandatory \naccreditation, etc. are  periodically reviewed with Vice Chancellors of Central Universities by \nUGC and Minister. \n \nAs regards implementation of reservation policy in Central Universities, University Grants \nCommission (UGC) issues instructions from time to time to all Central Universities for : \n \ni)  Implementation of SC/ST/PWD/OBC Reservation Policy of the Govt./UGC \nii) Display of reservation roster on University website and \niii) Filling up of remaining identified reserved vacancies of these categories in teaching \nand non-teaching posts. \n(iv) While releasing the grant to CUs, it is mentioned in all sanction letters from \ntime to time with regard to reservation of SC/ST/OBC/PwD posts and fill up the \nbacklog vacancies. \n \nThe guidelines issued by UGC in this regard are followed by the Central Universities.  \n \n\n-2- \n \n(d): Improvement in the performance of Central Universities is an on -going process.   The \nschemes and programmes introduced by the UGC for the improvement of quality in the \nCentral Universities include:- \ni) Introduction of Semester System, \nii) Periodic updation of curriculum \niii) Introduction of choice-based credit system, \niv) Prescription of minimum qualification for appointment of teachers and other \nacademic staff, \nv) Better pay scale and promotional avenues to teachers of the Central Universities to \nattract young talent into teaching profession \nvi) Introduction of mandatory assessment and accreditation \nvii) Establishment of Internal Quality Assurance Cell, \nviii) Introduction of Faculty Recharge programme to augment research and teaching \nresources,  \nix) Financial support under the scheme of University with Potential for Excellence. \n \n***** \n \n \n  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|13|UNSTARRED |315", "t": "Salt Production", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \nDEPARTMENT OF INDUSTRIAL POLICY & PROMOTION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 315. \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, THE 18TH DECEMBER,  2017. \n \nSALT PRODUCTION \n \n315.  SHRI RAHUL KASWAN: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY be pleased to state: \n                          वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग मंत्री \n(a) whether sufficient amount of salt is being produced in the country including \nfrom Rajasthan; \n \n(b) if so, whether the Government is conducting any survey and research  to \nfurther increase the production of salt in the country and if so, the details \nthereof along with the main features of the current salt policy; \n \n(c) whether the Government is considering to formulate any new scheme for the \ndevelopment of salt industry and i f so, the details thereof along with its main \nfeatures; \n \n(d) the details of the welfare funds/financial assistance provided to the workers \nengaged in salt industry and their families during the last three years and the \ncurrent year, State/UT-wise; and \n \n(e) the steps being taken for the welfare of salt workers in the country? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nवाणिज्‍ य‍एवं‍उद्योग मंत्रालय‍में‍राज्‍ यमंत्री‍(श्री सी.आर.‍चौधरी)‍ \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE \nIN THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRI C.R. CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a):  Yes, Madam. \n \n(b):  No, Madam. \n \n(c):  No, Madam. \n(d) & (e): The details of welfare funds/financial assistance for the welfare \nactivities of workers engaged in the salt industry along with the steps \ntaken for  the welfare activities is annexed herewith. \n***** \n\nAnnexure \n \nANNEXURE REFFERED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (d) & (e ) OF  THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 315 FOR ANSWER ON 18.12.2017. \n \n \nFinancial Assistance given by the Salt Department for the execution of Labour Welfare \nWorks for salt workers \n \n(Expenditure in Rupees) \nS. \nNo.  \nName of the \nSalt Producing \nState \n2014-15 \n \n2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 \n  Plan Non-Plan Plan Non-Plan Plan Non-Plan  \n1. Gujarat 1,50,000 26,96,898  3,96,976 2,71,451 0 Rs. 30 lakh has \nbeen \nearmarked \nunder the head \n“Scheme for \nSalt Workers”.  \n2. Karnataka  1,37,775 1,08,000  17,500  0 \n3. Maharashtra 3,51,755 81,000  87,500  35,000 \n4. West Bengal - 25,000  11,000  0 \n5 Odisha 2,51,776 1,49,000  92,000  0 \n6 Andhra Pradesh 7,09,720 9,81,306      8,85,826 9,14,726 6,87,403 0 \n7 Tamil Nadu  5,56,148 9,49,589   7,22,000 4,19,101 1,40,000 \n8 Rajasthan 2,62,384 10,90,706  29,000  69,905 \n9 Goa -      \n Total 24,19,558 60,81,499 18,85,000* 22,70,702 13,77,955 2,44,905 - \n* This includes Rs.10.00 lakhs which has been paid towards the Central Salt and Marine Chemical Research Institute, \nBhavnagar for conducting two training programmes for the Master Trainers (each training programme for 20 master \ntrainers costs Rs. 5.00 lakhs). \n \nDetails of steps/ schemes for welfare of salt workers: \n \nOffice of Salt Commissioner (SCO), Jaipur has inter -alia taken various steps for welfare of \nsalt workers by extending financial assistance for executing welfare schemes for them as \nfollows: \n \n Water supply schemes including provisions of water coolers, storage tanks, water \ntankers mounted on trailers.  \n Construction of labour rest shed, crèches, toilets etc. \n Provision of augmentation of medical facilities including conducting general health \ncum eye camps. \n Provision of community centers and recreation facilities including organization of \nsports meets, installation of TV sets etc. \n Provision of augmentation of educational facilities for the children of salt workers \nemployed in the salt industry including grant of rewards to meritorious children of salt \nworkers for purchase of books etc.  \n Labour housing, subject to the provision of the schemes formulated in this regard. \n Provision of supplying bi-cycles for salt workers.  \n Provision for supplying safety  kits containing gloves, cap, goggles, gumboots etc. to \nthe salt workers.   \n******  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|13|UNSTARRED |316", "t": "e-Biz Portal", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \nDEPARTMENT OF INDUSTRIAL POLICY & PROMOTION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 316. \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, THE 18TH DECEMBER,  2017. \n \ne-BIZ PORTAL \n316.  DR. KIRIT P. SOLANKI: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY be pleased to state: \n                        वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग मंत्री \n(a) the details of the services including State level services currently offered on the e -Biz \nportal of the Government; \n \n(b) whether the e -Biz portal has experienced any technical glitches and if so, the details \nthereof and the corrective steps taken by the Government to prevent such technical \nglitches in the future; and \n \n(c) whether the e-Biz portal has improved the ease of doing business in the country and if \nso, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nवाणिज्‍ य एवं उद्योग‍मंत्रालय‍में‍ राज्यमंत्री (श्री सी.आर. चौधरी)  \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE \nIN THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRI C.R. CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a): The details of the services including State level services currently offered on the e-Biz \nportal of Department of Industrial Policy & Promotion are given below:- \n \n List of 