T.S.R.  \nSubramanian Committee in the New Education Policy -2016 and if so, the details  of  the \nrecommendations that were accepted and implemented; \n \n(b) whether the Government has not accepted any of the recommendations and if so, the reasons \ntherefor; \n \n(c) the reasons for not publishing the complete report of  the  2016  draft  in  the public domain; \nand  \n \n(d)  whether  the  Government  intends to Publish the complete report and if so, the details for the \nestimated time frame for  the  same  and  if  not,  the  reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n \n(Dr. SATYA PAL SINGH) \n \n(a) to (d) : The Government is in the process of formulating a New Education Policy  for which \ninitially, it had constituted a Committee for Evolution of the New Education Policy  in October \n2015 under the C hairmanship of Shri T.S.R. Subramanian, former Cabinet Secretar y to the \nGovernment of India  which submitted its report in May, 2016. The Report of the Committee is \navailable on the website of NUEPA , which was the Committee’s Secretariat , and can be accessed \nat http://www.nuepa.org/New/download/NEP2016/ReportNEP.pdf. \nAfter perusal of the report of the Committee and the based on reports of various consultations as \nwell as views and comments received, the Ministry prepared “Some Inputs for the D raft National \nEducation Policy, 2016 ” which is  available on the MHRD website at \nhttp://mhrd.gov.in/sites/upload_files/mhrd/files/Inputs_Draft_NEP_2016.pdf. Both these reports \nhave been treated as inputs for education policy formulation.  \nThe exercise of preparing a New Education Policy is still ongoing as the Government has recently \nconstituted a Co mmittee for preparation of the D raft National Education Policy under the \nChairmanship of Dr. K. Kasturirangan, which is due to submit its report soon. \n \n********** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|13|UNSTARRED |329", "t": "Petrochemical Investors Conclave 2017", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.329  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18th DECEMBER, 2017 \n \nPETROCHEMICAL INVESTORS CONCLAVE 2017 \n \n 329: SHRI J.C. DIVAKAR REDDY: \n \nपैट्रोल ियम और प्राकृ तिक गैस मंत्री \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has held Petrochemical Investors Conclave 2017 and also \nHydrocarbon related conference in Visakhapatnam, Andhra Pradesh recently; and   \n(b) if so, the details thereof and issues discussed therein and the outcome thereof?  \n \nANSWER \nपैट्रोलियम और प्राक ृ लिक गैस मंत्री (श्री धमेन्द्र प्रधान) \nMINISTER OF PETROELUM & NATURAL GAS \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) & (b): Petrochemical Investors Conclave 2017 was held at Bhubaneshwar on \n16.11.2017.   Over 750 delegates attended the Conclave.  During the conclave, three \nMoUs were signed, each with I nstitute of Chemical Technology (I CT), Mumbai, MCPI \nPrivate Ltd, West Bengal  and Odisha Industrial Infrastructure Development Corporation \n(IDCO), Odisha by Indian Oil Corporation Ltd. \nFurther,    21st Refinery Technology Meet was organised at Visakhapatnam in April, 2017 \nwith the theme “Refining to Petrochemicals -The way Ahead”. Large number of \ndelegates/speakers/ senior executives from Oil Industry around the world participated in \nthe Meet. 74 number s of technical papers, including 47 papers from Global leaders in \nRefining and Petrochemical Technology were presented. The Meet provided opportunity \nfor exchange of latest technological advances and best practices followed worldwide. \n \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|13|UNSTARRED |33", "t": "Stem Cell Research", "head": "������������������� �\n���������������������������� �\n��� ������ �\n���������������������� ���\n������������������ �����������\n�\n�������������������� �������� �\n������ �������������������������� �\n����������������������������������������� �\n�\n�����������������������������������������������