 \nachieved and the action taken against the  guilty under the Prevention of Children  \nfrom Sexual Offences Act, 2012 (POCSO)  Act, during each of the last three years \nand the current year, crime and State-wise including Rajasthan; \n \n(b) whether the Government has  conducted any study about the efficacy of  the \nPOCSO Act, 2012 and if so, the details and findings thereof; and \n \n(c) th e budgetary allocation made and  its utilization for the implementation of  \nPOCSO Act during the said period, State-wise including Rajasthan? \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a): As per the information provided by the National Crime Records Bureau \n(NCRB), State/UT -wise cases registered, cases in which trials were completed, \ncases convicted, conviction rate and persons arrested under Protection of \nChildren from Sexual Offences Act, 2012 including Rajasthan, during 2014-2016 is \nenclosed as Annexure-I. \n(b) & (c): Protection of Children from Sexual Offences (POCSO) Act 2012, came \ninto force on 14 th November, 2012. The Government has not conducted any study \non it s efficacy as yet. As per the available information, there is no separate \nbudget allocated for the implementation of POCSO Act. \n***** \n \n \n\n                         \n \n \n \nAnnexure-I \nState/UT-wise Cases Registered (CR),Cases in which Trials were completed (CTC),Cases Convicted (CON),Conviction Rate (CVR) and Persons Arrested (PAR) under Protection of Children from Sexual \nOffences Act (POCSO) during 2014 \nSL State/UT Child Rape (Sec. 4 & 6 POCSO)/ Sec. 376 IPC Sexual Assault of Children(Sec 8 & 10 POCSO)/ \nSec. 354 IPC Sexual Harassment(Sec.12 POCSO)/ Sec.509 IPC Other Sections of POCSO POCSO r/w IPC (TOTAL) \nCR CTC CON CVR PAR CR CTC CON CVR PAR CR CTC CON CVR PAR CR CTC CON CVR PAR CR CTC CON CVR PAR \n1 Andhra Pradesh 477 185 13 7.0 638 274 64 7 10.9 285 75 24 8 33.3 127 106 17 1 5.9 113 932 290 29 10.0 116